The desktop application and its installers, exercised end to end on a real
machine: the Windows NSIS installer registering the recorder service, the
installed product recording real adapter changes and exporting a bundle
through its own API, the Linux desktop bundles built and installed on
Ubuntu, and the screenshots under docs/screenshots/ taken from the
installed application.

## Where this ran

The same separate, physical Windows 11 test machine as logs 25 and 26
(Windows 11 Home 26200, admin SSH with key auth), never the build machine.
Windows side for the installer and the live tests; its WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04
(systemd 255) for the Linux desktop bundles. The adapters used are the
ones those logs already established as safe: `Ethernet 2` (ifIndex 16, a
VirtualBox host-only adapter with real link state, 192.168.56.1/24) for
disable/enable, addresses and routes; the SSH path was never touched.
Everything the tests added was removed afterwards and re-checked: the
service, the install directory, `%ProgramData%\NetRewind`, the work
directory, the Ubuntu build toolchain and its 342 apt packages, the
scheduled task used to show progress on the machine's own screen.

Paths below are shown with `<work dir>` for the temporary directory the
files were copied into, and `<hostname>` where the recorder printed the
machine name.

