The disable, the addresses and routes that left with it, the enable, and
the address and route added and removed by hand are all in the record, in
order, with the right causes. The bundle the CLI exported is the same
format the desktop application opens (`bundle-open-en.png` below shows a
bundle exported this way, opened in the application).

The installed application was then started in the interactive session on
that machine and the screenshots under `docs/screenshots/` taken from it,
in live mode against the installed service (`health-live-*`,
`timeline-live-en`, `rules-live-en`, `evidence-live-en`,
`diagnostics-live-en`), with the exported bundle open (`bundle-open-en`),
and through the first-run wizard in both languages (`wizard-*`). Each
image was checked before being kept: no taskbar, no window other than the
application, observer id `workstation`, no account name or address that
identifies the machine.

## 5. Linux desktop bundles

Built on the test machine's Ubuntu 24.04 with `npm run tauri build`
(Tauri 2, webkit2gtk 4.1), with the recorder staged as a resource by
`make desktop-resources`. The first build came out under Tauri's default
naming, which turns the product name into `net-rewind`:

    -rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 77974008 Sep 14 11:36 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/appimage/NetRewind_1.0.0_amd64.AppImage
    -rw-r--r-- 1 root root  2865914 Sep 14 11:20 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/rpm/NetRewind-1.0.0-1.x86_64.rpm
    -rw-r--r-- 1 root root  2865182 Sep 14 11:20 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/deb/NetRewind_1.0.0_amd64.deb
    --- .deb metadata ---
    Package: net-rewind
    Version: 1.0.0
    Depends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0
    Recommends: netrewind
    Section: net
    --- install the desktop .deb, launch headlessly (expect a display error, not a missing library) ---
    installed
    launch exit=0
    missing shared libraries: 0
    removed the desktop .deb again

`desktop/src-tauri/tauri.linux.conf.json` (a Linux-only overlay) now sets
the product name to `netrewind-desktop`, with a custom `.desktop` entry
template so the menu still reads "NetRewind"; the AppImage build needs
`xdg-utils` on the build host. Rebuilt with the overlay:

    -rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 77974008 Sep 14 11:45 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/appimage/netrewind-desktop_1.0.0_amd64.AppImage
    -rw-r--r-- 1 root root  2865884 Sep 14 11:44 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/deb/netrewind-desktop_1.0.0_amd64.deb
    -rw-r--r-- 1 root root  2866607 Sep 14 11:44 src-tauri/target/release/bundle/rpm/netrewind-desktop-1.0.0-1.x86_64.rpm
    Package: netrewind-desktop
    Version: 1.0.0
    Recommends: netrewind
