    7746d288fb94c6dc49fc9a891d579640344d25942da39eaa76f47a69ddcb2aaf  netrewind-desktop-1.0.0-1.x86_64.rpm
    d1c69fbbe9dfd8cceb0992f06552d0f1572424e1aaf50d2193432d5bc1773fdc  netrewind-desktop_1.0.0_amd64.AppImage
    5f8c24fb07a4c3ba8e9f8a8be0d294c98a38f024d69dfb8063033a15b0d889f5  netrewind-desktop_1.0.0_amd64.deb

The `.deb` was installed on that Ubuntu and the binary launched from a
session without a display: it fails on the display, not on a missing
library (`missing shared libraries: 0`), then the package was removed.
Not done here: running the Linux desktop application against a live
recorder on a Linux desktop session - the live-mode code path is the same
one the Windows run above exercised (the only platform-specific part is
the transport, a Unix socket instead of a named pipe, which log 11 covers).
The `.rpm` was built but not installed on an rpm-based host in this run.
